course: dictionary
lesson: 7608
title: Prisms and light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A prism has two meanings. In maths, a prism is a solid shape with two ends that are the same flat shape, joined by flat sides. In science, a prism is a block of clear glass or plastic that splits light into colours.
explain: The words around it show which meaning is used. «A triangular prism» or «a rectangular prism» is a maths shape, because the word before "prism" names its end shape. «A glass prism bends each colour by a different amount» is the science meaning.
explain: Test your meaning in the sentence. «White sunlight is really a mixture of all the colours, and when it passes through a glass prism they fan out into a rainbow.» So a prism spreads white light out into a rainbow of colours.
fact: A prism is a solid shape with two ends that are the same flat shape.
fact: A rectangular prism is also called a cuboid.
fact: In science, a prism is a block of glass or clear plastic, often triangular.
fact: «A prism splits white light into the colours of the rainbow.»
fact: Newton showed that a second prism could mix the colours back into white.
exercise: «A prism splits white light into the colours of the rainbow.» What does a prism do to white light? | Makes it darker | Stops it completely | Turns it into sound | *Splits it into the colours of the rainbow
exercise: «A triangular prism» is a shape in maths. What are its two ends like? | *The same flat shape | Round like a coin | Always square | Pointed to a single tip
exercise: «A glass prism bends violet light most and red light least.» Which colour does the prism bend least? | Blue | *Red | Violet | Yellow
test: «Split starlight into a rainbow with a prism and you see thin dark lines, like a barcode.» What do the lines tell us? | *What the star is made of | How far away the star is | The star's name | Whether the star is hot
test: In maths, how do you find the volume of a prism? | Count the faces | *Multiply the area of the end by the length | Count the vertices | Add all the edges together
exam: «White sunlight is really a mixture of all the colours, and when it passes through a raindrop or a glass prism each colour bends by a slightly different amount.» Why does a prism make a rainbow? | Because the prism paints the light red | Because the prism adds new colours to the light | Because prisms are always coloured | *Because white light is a mix of colours, and each bends by a different amount
